  "scientific_limits": {
    "en": "Hypothetical whole-animal Megarachne servinei, a non-marine aquatic eurypterid, not a giant spider. Fossils constrain the anterior shield, enlarged first two tergites and partial limbs; posterior body, telson, limb endings, depth and pose are inferred. Colour and the roughly 0.54 m body-length target are reconstruction choices, not complete-specimen measurements.",
    "zh": "Megarachne servinei 的假说性全身复原，属非海相水生广翅鲎，并非巨型蜘蛛。化石约束前部背甲、增大的前两节背板及部分附肢；后躯、尾剑、足端、体厚与姿势为推测。颜色及约0.54米体长目标属复原选择，非完整标本实测。"
  },
  "frozen_budget": {
    "max_triangles": 16000,
    "max_materials": 8,
    "max_primitives": 72,
    "max_glb_bytes": 3000000,
    "target_triangles": [
      6000,
      11000
    ],
    "rationale": "Eight readable articulated limbs, profile-based armor plates, ribbed second tergite and a tapered inferred tail need more silhouette geometry than a simple prop. This is a practical ceiling, not a target to fill. Group cosmetic parts by semantic region and material without sacrificing editability."
  },
